l,"transcript_cfo_tone":null,"transcript_take":"Q1 FY2026 call (2026-04-24): revenue +4.3%, adjusted EBITDA +~2% (margin -50bps), adjusted dil EPS +~11%; but volumes softened - same-facility admissions +0.9%, inpatient surgeries -0.3%, outpatient surgeries -1.7% - on a mild respiratory season (respiratory admissions -42%) and a January winter storm (~$180M combined EBITDA drag). A higher-than-expected supplemental-payment benefit (~$200M vs $80M expected, Georgia grandfathered approval + Texas Atlas reinstatement) mostly offset it and FY2026 guidance was reaffirmed. Real positives (EPS growth, reaffirmed guide, supplemental upside) against real negatives (surgery/margin softness, ~$150M exchange impact, looming eEPTC/SDP policy cliff).","mda_take":"FY2025 10-K (filed 2026-02-10): a record year - revenue +7.1% to $75.600B, net income $6.784B ($28.33 dil EPS vs $22.00), same-facility equivalent admissions +2.4% and revenue per equivalent admission +4.1%, salaries/benefits down to 43.5% of revenue and supplies 15.0%; $10.067B buybacks + $679M dividends. Consistent-or-better on the period, but the MD&A explicitly discloses 2026 headwinds: expiration of enhanced premium tax credits at end-2025, the 2025 Federal Budget Act state-directed-payment (SDP) limits, and an expected SDP revenue decline in 2026.","mda_filing_date":"2026-02-10","mda_filing_form":"10-K","mda_filing_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/860730/000119312526044769/hca-20251231.htm","confidence_rule":"BUY_DIP","historical_hit_rate_60d":74.4,"historical_avg_alpha_60d":1.09,"historical_n":39,"historical_alpha_n":39,"historical_hit_rate_vs_spy_60d":53.8,"historical_evidence_status":"supported_descriptive_sample","historical_evidence_version":"timing-evidence-2","historical_sample_note":"Descriptive price-rule replay; n counts events, not independent observations. Absolute hit rate is not probability of beating SPY; no calibrated return forecast.","conv_band_margin":0.15,"conv_fund_band":"Neutral","